BBUUGGSS
     The nnvvddiimmmm driver does not utilize the Block Window interface, so if a
     write to an NVDIMM is interrupted due to a system crash or power outage,
     the corresponding page might be left in a partially updated state.

     There is no support for Device-Specific Methods (DSM), used to report and
     control device health and wearing.

     The driver depends on the pmap_largemap(9) pmap interface, which is cur‐
     rently only implemented on amd64.  The interface can be only reasonable
     implemented on 64bit architectures.

